@page
@model PrivacyModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy";
}

@* SHARED PAGE. Linked from the footer of every page, so it is the one place
   that explains what the system holds about a student. It replaced the
   placeholder text the project template ships with.

   Written plainly and kept honest: it describes what the code actually does. If
   a feature changes what we store, this page changes with it. *@

<div class="page-header">
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p class="page-subtitle">What Grantify stores about you, and who can see it.</p>
</div>

<div class="row">
    <div class="col-lg-8">

        <h2 class="section-title">What we hold</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>Your name, email address and password. The password is stored only as a hash, never as text.</li>
            <li>The academic and household details you enter on your profile: course, institution, CGPA and monthly household income.</li>
            <li>The applications you send, and any supporting documents you upload.</li>
            <li>A record of every action a scholarship officer takes on your application, including who did it and when.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 class="section-title">Why we hold it</h2>
        <p>
            Your CGPA and household income are compared against each scholarship's published rules
            to work out whether you qualify. Your documents are read by a scholarship officer to
            check that what you entered is accurate. Nothing is used for any other purpose.
        </p>

        <h2 class="section-title">Who can see it</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>You</strong> can see everything on your own account, and nothing on anyone else's.</li>
            <li><strong>Scholarship officers</strong> can see applications and the documents attached to them, so they can review them.</li>
            <li><strong>Administrators</strong> can see accounts and roles, and totals across the system. They do not open your documents.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
            Officers keep working notes on documents. Those notes stay between officers — the only
            thing sent to you is a decision on your application, together with its reason.
        </p>

        <h2 class="section-title">Your documents</h2>
        <p>
            Uploaded files are kept in private storage, never in a public folder. They cannot be
            reached by guessing a web address: every download goes through a check that you own
            the application the file belongs to.
        </p>

        <h2 class="section-title">Keeping and removing data</h2>
        <p>
            Applications and their history are kept as a record of decisions made, so a result can
            always be traced back to the officer who made it. If you no longer want an account,
            ask a scholarship administrator to deactivate it.
        </p>

        <p class="cell-sub">
            Grantify is a student project built for the module CT071-3-3-DDAC at Asia Pacific
            University. It is not a live scholarship service.
        </p>

    </div>
</div>
